## Known lessons learned to document (security.md / lessons-learned.md)

- RDS password was set manually; best practice is RDS-managed credentials in Secrets Manager (auto-rotation, no plaintext exposure).
- `SecretsManagerReadWrite` and `AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess` are broad managed policies; production would use inline policies scoped to specific ARNs (least privilege).
- A refactor that crossed two files (app.py + bootstrap) introduced a `NameError` caught only by running the code — the argument for the CI lint planned in Phase 5.
- RDS is single-AZ for cost; architecture is "Multi-AZ ready" — promotion is a one-click toggle with no app change.
